WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:11.393
In tutorial 6.6, you'll send an
approved page to your CMS as a draft,

00:00:11.443 --> 00:00:13.292
and follow it until it's live.

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:18.178
First, approve the page in its
report. Once it's approved,

00:00:18.228 --> 00:00:22.036
Publish to your CMS appears
right under Approve and publish.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:28.695
Pages go to your CMS as drafts by default,
so nothing goes public by accident.

00:00:28.745 --> 00:00:34.227
Click Send to CMS as draft. Publish live
sends it straight to your live website.

00:00:35.192 --> 00:00:39.392
On a page you've sent, the card shows
where it is, like Live in Webhook,

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:41.272
with Open it to see the page.

00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:47.842
History lists every send, who made it,
and when: here, a draft by Alex Morgan,

00:00:47.892 --> 00:00:49.810
made live by Sana Qureshi.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.908
Changed the page later? Update the
live page sends the new version.

00:00:56.259 --> 00:01:00.294
Published it yourself in your
CMS? Click Check if it is live,

00:01:00.344 --> 00:01:03.270
and Alaventra checks the
page and starts tracking it.

00:01:04.235 --> 00:01:07.610
So every page you approve reaches
your website the same way,

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.383
and you always know where it is.

00:01:10.408 --> 00:01:14.883
So, to recap: approve the page,
send it to your CMS as a draft,

00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:18.671
see where it is and who sent it, then
update it or check that it's live.

00:01:19.655 --> 00:01:24.605
Your page is in your CMS. Next, read
a written page before you publish it,

00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:26.659
in tutorial 6.7.
